worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_web_providers_and_wasm_calls.js"
  ceiling 1168
  rationale "Fetch and navigation answers, the WebAssembly engine calls and the web-search providers. Issue #658 cut this module out of one oversized worker file by line count; R1188-U5 named it after what it holds. Its ceiling falls as its logic moves into js/wasm-worker. Ceiling moved 1185 to 1191 when plan 10 L20 retired conversational phrase families onto declared roles. Lowered to 1164 for issue #918 (2026-10-08): the fetch, navigation and frame-policy wording and the Wikinews fallback description are seeded web_* responses (data/seed/multilingual-responses-synthesis.lino), which the native url_navigate row renders too. Ceiling moved 1164 to 1166 (R1188-U5): the first comment lines say what the module holds. Ceiling moved 1166 to 1168 (R1188-U18, 2026-10-09): tryFetch first offers the prompt to tryPageFormalization (formal_ai_worker_page_formalization.js), so "formalize <url>" answers the fetched page as statements, as native answer_http_fetch_url does."
